WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:06.675
P2.2 · Working capital: DSO, DPO, DIO and trailing windows

2
00:00:07.825 --> 00:00:13.443
DSO, DPO and DIO estimate days to collect, to sell stock, and to pay.

3
00:00:13.493 --> 00:00:18.284
The cash conversion cycle is DSO plus DIO minus DPO.

4
00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:22.913
K-φ uses a three-month trailing window by default.

5
00:00:22.963 --> 00:00:25.878
A single month can mislead in either direction.

6
00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:32.482
DSO is a pointer. When it moves, open the receivables by customer.

7
00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:38.684
Next: P2.3  Covenants and headroom

